module System/Numerics

# `Int` to a fixed-width integer without failing: `n.to_wrap[U8]()` keeps the value modulo 2^8 read in the target's
# range, `n.to_clamp[U8]()` gives the nearest value the target holds. `n.to[U8]()` crashes when the value does not fit.

### Converts to `S8` modulo 2^8: the value read in the `S8` range, as the low 8 bits of two's complement.
### :returns: This value modulo 2^8 as a `S8`.
routine Int.to_wrap[S8]() -> S8
    var low = me.mod(other: "256".to[Int]())
    if low > "127".to[Int]()
        return (low - "256".to[Int]()).to[S8]()
    return low.to[S8]()

### Converts to `S8`, giving the nearest `S8` when this value is outside its range.
### :returns: This value, or `S8`'s bound on the side it lies past.
routine Int.to_clamp[S8]() -> S8
    if me < "-128".to[Int]()
        return -128
    if me > "127".to[Int]()
        return 127
    return me.to[S8]()

### Converts to `S16` modulo 2^16: the value read in the `S16` range, as the low 16 bits of two's complement.
### :returns: This value modulo 2^16 as a `S16`.
routine Int.to_wrap[S16]() -> S16
    var low = me.mod(other: "65536".to[Int]())
    if low > "32767".to[Int]()
        return (low - "65536".to[Int]()).to[S16]()
    return low.to[S16]()

### Converts to `S16`, giving the nearest `S16` when this value is outside its range.
### :returns: This value, or `S16`'s bound on the side it lies past.
routine Int.to_clamp[S16]() -> S16
    if me < "-32768".to[Int]()
        return -32768
    if me > "32767".to[Int]()
        return 32767
    return me.to[S16]()

