### Converts to `S256` modulo 2^256: the value read in the `S256` range, as the low 256 bits of two's complement.
### :returns: This value modulo 2^256 as a `S256`.
routine Int.to_wrap[S256]() -> S256
    var low = me.mod(other: "115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639936".to[Int]())
    if low > "57896044618658097711785492504343953926634992332820282019728792003956564819967".to[Int]()
        return (low - "115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639936".to[Int]()).to[S256]()
    return low.to[S256]()

### Converts to `S256`, giving the nearest `S256` when this value is outside its range.
### :returns: This value, or `S256`'s bound on the side it lies past.
routine Int.to_clamp[S256]() -> S256
    if me < "-57896044618658097711785492504343953926634992332820282019728792003956564819968".to[Int]()
        return -57896044618658097711785492504343953926634992332820282019728792003956564819968
    if me > "57896044618658097711785492504343953926634992332820282019728792003956564819967".to[Int]()
